From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:40:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] feat(license): request form (contact + requested days)
 delivered as an encrypted .zip with a unique name

VERSION: 1.1 (2026-10-16)  1.1 = Persian letters kept in the file-name slug
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0021)

The admin now fills in a short form on Settings > License before asking for a
license: the name the license is for (legal or personal), the representative's
first and last name, a phone number, the requested duration in days and a note
for the supplier. These go INSIDE the X25519-encrypted, server-signed request
payload, so only the vendor can read them.

The request is handed back as a .zip whose single stored (uncompressed) entry
is the armored request, so the vendor tool reads the armored block straight
from the zip bytes without a zip library. The file name carries the customer
slug, the request time (to the second) and a short install id, so every
request file of a customer is unique:
  kms-license-request-<slug>-<YYYYMMDDHHMMSS>-<installId8>.zip

Files (7; N = new, M = modified, D = deleted):
  M server/license/format.ts
  M server/license/state.ts
  N server/license/zip.ts
  M server/routes/api/license/schema.ts
  M server/routes/api/license/license.ts
  M app/scenes/Settings/License.tsx
  M shared/i18n/locales/fa_IR/translation.json

